 little confusing given that `p_` is for all input parameters in most of the engine. And folks will need to remember this rule going forward, so we don't just undo the clean-up that this PR is doing.\n\nThis is especially confusing in these two specific functions, which have an argument of each possible type in the same signature.\n\nWhat if we always removed `p_` and just kept `r_` for output parameters? That feels like a simpler rule to remember and enforce","created_at":"2026-04-03T12:58:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-03T12:58:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115938#discussion_r3032769805","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115938","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3032769805"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115938#discussion_r3032769805"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115938"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3032769805/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":605,"start_side":"LEFT","line":null,"original_line":606,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3085706202","pull_request_review_id":4112706113,"id":3085706202,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc637CPa","diff_hunk":"@@ -602,8 +602,8 @@ Error StreamPeerExtension::put_partial_data(const uint8_t *p_data, int p_bytes,\n void StreamPeerExtension::_bind_methods() {\n \tGDVIRTUAL_BIND(_get_data, \"r_buffer\", \"r_bytes\", \"r_received\");\n \tGDVIRTUAL_BIND(_get_partial_data, \"r_buffer\", \"r_bytes\", \"r_received\");\n-\tGDVIRTUAL_BIND(_put_data, \"p_data\", \"p_bytes\", \"r_sent\");\n-\tGDVIRTUAL_BIND(_put_partial_data, \"p_data\", \"p_bytes\", \"